description.content:
Verify Verifiable Presentation
This endpoint is used to verify a Verifiable Presentation (VP) for a specific tenant and community. It allows clients to submit a VP and receive a verification status in return, confirming whether the VP is valid.

Request
HTTP Method: POST
Endpoint: {{client_api}}/vcs/tenant/:tenantID/community/:communityID/vp/verify

Request Body
The request body must be in JSON format and should contain the following structure:

{
  "vp": {
    "@context": [<Array of Context URLs>],
    "type": [<Array of Types>],
    "verifiableCredential": [
      {
        "@context": [<Array of Context URLs>],
        "id": "<Credential ID>",
        "type": [<Array of Types>],
        "issuer": {
          "id": "<Issuer ID>",
          "tenantId": "<Tenant ID>",
          "communityId": "<Community ID>"
        },
        "issuanceDate": "<Issuance Date>",
        "expirationDate": "<Expiration Date>",
        "credentialSubject": {
          "firstName": "<First Name>",
          "id": "<Subject ID>",
          "publicKey": "<Public Key>"
        },
        "proof": {
          "type": "<Proof Type>",
          "created": "<Creation Date>",
          "verificationMethod": "<Verification Method>",
          "proofPurpose": "<Proof Purpose>",
          "proofValue": "<Proof Value>"
        },
        "statusUrl": "<Status URL>"
      }
    ],
    "proof": {
      "type": "<Proof Type>",
      "created": "<Creation Date>",
      "verificationMethod": "<Verification Method>",
      "proofPurpose": "<Proof Purpose>",
      "proofValue": "<Proof Value>"
    }
  }
}

Response
The response will be in JSON format and will indicate the verification result along with the status of the verifiable credentials. The structure of the response is as follows:

{
  "verified": <Boolean>,
  "vc_status": [
    {
      "subject": {
        "did": "<Subject DID>",
        "publicKey": "<Subject Public Key>"
      },
      "type": [<Array of Types>],
      "_id": "<Credential ID>",
      "vcID": "<Verifiable Credential ID>",
      "tenantId": "<Tenant ID>",
      "communityId": "<Community ID>",
      "proof": {
        "type": "<Proof Type>",
        "created": "<Creation Date>",
        "verificationMethod": "<Verification Method>",
        "proofPurpose": "<Proof Purpose>",
        "proofValue": "<Proof Value>"
      },
      "issueTS": <Issue Timestamp>,
      "expiryTS": <Expiry Timestamp>,
      "status": "<Status>",
      "issuer": {
        "id": "<Issuer ID>",
        "tenantId": "<Tenant ID>",
        "communityId": "<Community ID>"
      }
    }
  ]
}

Example Responses

{"verified": true,"vc_status": [ { "subject": { "did": "", "publicKey": "" }, "type": [""], "_id": "", "vcID": "", "tenantId": "", "communityId": "", "proof": { "type": "", "created": "", "verificationMethod": "", "proofPurpose": "", "proofValue": "" }, "issueTS": 0, "expiryTS": 0, "status": "", "issuer": { "id": "", "tenantId": "", "communityId": "" } }]}

This endpoint is crucial for ensuring the integrity and validity of verifiable credentials within the specified tenant and community.
